      "function": "magiccheck",
      "line": null,
      "code": "for (idx = 0; m->str_range == 0 || idx < m->str_range; idx++) { if (slen + idx > ms->search.s_len) return 0; v = file_strncmp(m->value.s, ms->search.s + idx, slen, m->str_flags); if (v == 0) { ms->search.offset += idx; ms->search.rm_len = ms->search.s_len - idx; break; } }",
      "note": "On the lex continuation `>3 search/1 >\\0  for %s`, the only comparison is against the byte `'r'` at offset 3, so `v` becomes positive. Because the one-byte range ends immediately afterward, control falls out of the loop instead of rejecting the rule. The later `>` relation then interprets that positive `v` as a successful match and reaches `mprint` with `rm_len` still taken from the earlier top-level lex match.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
